de Quality and Handling Expert Impressions Critics Praise Real-World Driving Trim Levels and Options Pricing and Value Ownership Experience Warranty and Maintenance Longevity and Resale Conclusion FAQs Introduction The 2021 Mercedes S-Class isnt just a luxury sedanits a flagship statement of what modern automotive innovation should be. Known for its refinement, cutting-edge technology, and sumptuous comfort, the S-Class has consistently raised the bar for whats expected in executive sedans. The 2021 model continues this tradition with dramatic design upgrades, an advanced MBUX infotainment system, and next-level driver-assistance features. This article comprehensively examines the 2021 Mercedes S-Class, examining every detail from design and engine to expert impressions and real-world performance. Category Details Model Name 2021 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Available Trims S 500 4MATIC, S 580 4MATIC Engine Options 3.0L I6 turbo w/ EQ Boost (429 hp), 4.0L V8 Biturbo w/ EQ Boost (496 hp) Torque 384 lb-ft (S 500), 516 lb-ft (S 580) Transmission 9-speed automatic Drivetrain Standard 4MATIC all-wheel drive 060 mph Time ~4.4 seconds (S 580) Top Speed Electronically limited to 130 mph Fuel Economy (MPG) ~1721 city / 2630 highway Exterior Design Sleek silhouette, Digital Light LEDs, the aerodynamic drag coefficient of 0.22 Interior Highlights Nappa leather, wood/aluminium trim, ambient lighting, panoramic sunroof Infotainment System 12.8 OLED touchscreen, MBUX 2.0, voice control, AR navigation Rear Seat Tech Up to 3 rear screens, rear MBUX tablet Driver Assistance Adaptive cruise, lane keep assist, emergency braking, rear-axle steering. Suspension System AIRMATIC with E-Active Body Control Rear-Axle Steering Yes, up to 10 rotation for a tighter turning radius Safety Innovations Pre-Safe Impulse Side, advanced airbag deployment Trim Options Executive Line, Warmth & Comfort, Night Package, Rear Entertainment Base Price ~$110,000 (S 500), ~$117,000 (S 580) Max Price (Fully Loaded) ~